## A grid is rows in a col

Put `<row>`s one under the other and every row is a line of equal parts. `size=` makes a part wider,
`halign` and `valign` align inside it.

<row>
  <text>
    ### One

    Plain text.
  </text>
  <col>
    <text>
      ### Two
    </text>

    <code lang=python>
      <frame>
        x = 1
      </frame>
      <frame>
        x = 2   # on the first click
      </frame>
    </code>
  </col>
  <text>
    ### Three

    Nothing special.
  </text>
</row>

<row>
  <col halign=end>
    <text>
      ### Four

      Right-aligned with `halign=end`.
    </text>
  </col>
  <col size=2>
    <text>
      ### Five (`size=2`)

      This part is twice as wide as a normal one.
    </text>
  </col>
</row>
